From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:35:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: apple,pmc: Allow nonposted-mmio

The T6040 device tree places its SoC blocks at the root instead of under
a simple-bus, because the boot loader edits several of them by path.
With no bus node to carry nonposted-mmio, the blocks that need
non-posted writes carry the property themselves, the PMC voter interface
among them.

The property has an effect there. Since commit 47026c4ffedd ("of:
address: Allow to specify nonposted-mmio per-device")
of_mmio_is_nonposted() checks the device node as well as its parent bus.
The OF core then flags the node's memory resources
IORESOURCE_MEM_NONPOSTED, and devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname(),
which the PMC driver uses for its voters and rails windows, maps them
with ioremap_np(). Dropping the property would turn these mappings into
posted ones, so the fix belongs in the binding, which does not allow the
property yet.

Allow nonposted-mmio, as the Apple DockChannel, ATC PHY and USB4 ACIO
bindings do.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 992e3fb1f6cde5c127d53a3b304edec48f514983)
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml
index cbe0bbec21..036902f365 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ properties:
       - const: voters
       - const: rails
 
+  nonposted-mmio: true
+
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
